values ('ap_precalculus', 1, '1.2', array['1.2']::text[], 'vocabulary', 'Rate of change at a point', 'The rate of change of a function at a point quantifies the rate at which output values would change were the input values to change at that point, and it can be approximated by average rates of change over small intervals containing the point, if such values exist.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-precalculus-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_precalculus-u1-r2-002; ced=1.2.A.2: "The rate of change of a function at a point quantifies the rate at which output values would change were the input values to change at that point."')
