values ('ap_precalculus', 1, '1.5', array['1.5', '1.8', '1.9', '1.10', '1.11']::text[], 'convention', 'Zeros and linear factors', 'If a is a zero of p (a root of p(x)=0), then for real a the expression (x-a) is a linear factor of p if and only if a is a zero, and a real zero gives an x-intercept at (a, 0).', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-precalculus-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_precalculus-u1-r1-020; ced=1.5.A.1 "(x - a) is a linear factor of p if and only if a is a zero of p"; 1.5.A.3')
