values ('ap_precalculus', 1, '1.5', array['1.5', '1.8']::text[], 'convention', 'Zeros as endpoints of inequality intervals', 'Real zeros of a polynomial can be endpoints of intervals satisfying polynomial inequalities, and for a rational function the real zeros of the numerator and denominator are endpoints or asymptotes for intervals satisfying r(x) ≥ 0 or r(x) ≤ 0.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-precalculus-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_precalculus-u1-r2-008; ced=1.5.A.3: "real zeros of a polynomial can be endpoints for intervals satisfying polynomial inequalities"; 1.8.A.2: "endpoints or asymptotes for intervals satisfying the rational function inequalities"')
